<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Why we're building Dental AI Assistant</h2>
  <p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    Front desk staff at a dental practice spend a surprising share of the day answering the same handful of questions&mdash;pricing, insurance, availability&mdash;while chairside care waits. We're building Dental AI Assistant to take that routine communication off a practice's plate entirely, so staff time shifts back toward patients instead of the phone.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-4 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">The problem</h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    Scheduling, pricing, and insurance questions were competing with in-chair patient care for staff attention, appointments were going unreminded, and satisfied patients rarely left a review unless someone followed up right after their visit.
  </p>
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-red-200 bg-red-50 p-6">
    <p class="mb-2 font-medium text-[#111827]">Where practice time actually goes:</p>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">
      <li>&bull; Calls stack up during office hours, competing with in-chair patient care</li>
      <li>&bull; No-shows go unmanaged without timely, personalized reminders</li>
      <li>&bull; Satisfied patients rarely leave a review unless someone follows up right after their visit</li>
      <li>&bull; Any solution has to fit inside HIPAA and existing practice management software, not around it</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-4 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">How we're building it</h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    We're building Dental AI Assistant as an always-on layer over the practice's existing systems: it answers routine patient questions instantly, books appointments against real provider and chair availability, and sends personalized, multi-channel follow-ups&mdash;all logged and auditable to stay HIPAA-compliant. It's running in private beta with select practices ahead of general availability.
  </p>
  <div class="space-y-3">
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-navy-100/60 bg-white p-5 shadow-subtle">
      <p class="mb-1 font-medium text-[#111827]">24/7 patient communication</p>
      <p class="text-[13.5px] text-[#6B7280]">Patients get instant, accurate answers about procedures, pricing, and availability at any hour&mdash;no calls stacking up in a voicemail box.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-navy-100/60 bg-white p-5 shadow-subtle">
      <p class="mb-1 font-medium text-[#111827]">Scheduling that considers the whole practice</p>
      <p class="text-[13.5px] text-[#6B7280]">Appointments are booked against treatment duration, provider availability, and patient preference together, not a single open slot.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-navy-100/60 bg-white p-5 shadow-subtle">
      <p class="mb-1 font-medium text-[#111827]">Compliance built in, not bolted on</p>
      <p class="text-[13.5px] text-[#6B7280]">Every patient communication is logged and auditable, with end-to-end encryption and BAA agreements, so it fits inside HIPAA requirements from the start.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-navy-100/60 bg-white p-5 shadow-subtle">
      <p class="mb-1 font-medium text-[#111827]">Runs alongside existing practice software</p>
      <p class="text-[13.5px] text-[#6B7280]">Integration is being built for Dentrix, Eaglesoft, and Open Dental, so practices don't have to change their system of record to use it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-4 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Where it stands today</h2>
